  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0181" xml:lang="en">
          <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00544/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_kline">
              <opener>
                <seg hand="#print_bryn_mawr_college">
                    <lb/>DEPARTMENT OF PHILOSOPHY
                  <orgName>
                    <lb/><rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_479">BRYN MAWR COLLEGE</rs>
                   </orgName>
                  <placeName>
                    <lb/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_738">BRYN MAWR, PA.</rs> 19010
                  </placeName>
                </seg>
                <dateline>
                  <date>
                    <lb/><space quantity="20" unit="char"/>August 28, 1972
                  </date>
                </dateline>
                <salute>
                  <lb/>Dear <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Mr. Auden</rs>,
                </salute>
              </opener>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="4" unit="char"/>As you may know, <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_759">Iosif Brodsky</rs> spent a <rs type="event" ref="#amp_event_id_523">week with <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_758"><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_760">us</rs></rs></rs> at
                <lb/>our lakeside cottage in the <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_739">Berkshires</rs> (July 21-27), during
                <lb/>which time he and I worked very hard on the final revisions
                <lb/>of my translations for the <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_519">Penguin volume</rs>.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>(It was during 
                <lb/>an afternoon nap in our tree-house that he dreamed vividly
                <lb/>of you and <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_4">Chester K.</rs>; the postcard was written as soon as
                <lb/>he got up.)
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="4" unit="char"/>The MS is now ready to go off to <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_56">London</rs>, except for the
                <lb/>translation of a new (1972) poem of 72 lines called <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">Candle</hi>-
                <lb/><hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">mas</hi>.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>(I'll send you a copy of that translation within the
                <lb/>next few days.)<space quantity="2" unit="char"/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_793">Nikos Stangos</rs> assures me that on a "special
                <lb/>schedule" the <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_519">book</rs> can be published in March, 1973.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="4" unit="char"/>I'm sending you herewith copies of several parts of the
                <lb/>final MS, viz.:
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="4" unit="char"/>(1) The Table of Contents -- as rearranged by <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_759">Iosif</rs>,
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>and with a few titles and first lines altered.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="4" unit="char"/>(2) Your <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_552">Foreword</rs>, retyped to take account of revisions
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>in several of the passages which you quote.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="4" unit="char"/>(3) The translations of three poems that you have al-
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>ready seen:
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>(a) <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">Enigma for an Angel</hi> -- because of important
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>revisions and a new 3-line variant
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>(b) <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline"><foreign xml:lang="de">Einem alten Architekten in Rom</foreign></hi> -- because of
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>extensive revisions and important footnotes.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>(c) <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">Two Hours in a Dry Reservoir</hi> -- because of 
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>important revisions, new footnotes, and the new
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>style -- which <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_759">Iosif</rs> urged on me -- of writing
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>the "German" words and phrases without either
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>italics or capitalized nouns (for the reasons,
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>see fn. 2).
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="4" unit="char"/>(4) The translations of six poems that you haven't yet
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>seen.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>(As you probably know, <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_555">Barbara Epstein</rs> plans
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>to <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_553">publish some of these</rs> in the <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline"><rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_362">New York Review of
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>Books</rs></hi>.)
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>(a) From <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">The School Anthology</hi>: <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">Albert Frolov</hi>
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>(b) From <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">Gorbunov and Gorchakov</hi>, Canto II
              </p>
            </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00545/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
            <div>
              <ab hand="#hand_blue_unident_0181">
                <lb/>51a
              </ab>
            </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00546/" ed="2r" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_kline">
              <ab>
                <lb/><space quantity="23" unit="char"/>- 2 -
              </ab>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>(c) From <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">Gorbunov and Gorchakov</hi>, Canto X
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>(d) <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline"><foreign xml:lang="la">Post Aetatem Nostram</foreign></hi>
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="7" unit="char"/>(e) <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline"><foreign xml:lang="fr">Nature Morte</foreign></hi><space quantity="2" unit="char"/>(you <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">may</hi> have seen this; a slightly
                <lb/><space quantity="11" unit="char"/>less thoroughly revised version appeared in <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_513"><hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">Satur</hi>-
                <lb/><space quantity="11" unit="char"/><hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">day Review</hi>: <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">The Arts</hi></rs>, August 12, 1972, p. 45)
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="8" unit="char"/>(f) <hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">Odysseus to Telemachus</hi>
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="7" unit="char"/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_759">Iosif</rs> and I would, of course, be delighted if you
                <lb/>should feel inspired by any of these poems to add either
                <lb/>new quotations or further comments to your a<unclear><add hand="#type_black_kline" place="superimposed">l</add></unclear>ready splendid
                <lb/><rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_552">Foreword</rs>.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>But if you shouldn't, we'll understand perfectly.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="3" unit="char"/>We are in any case enormously grateful to you for your
                <lb/>warm and generous help and encouragement to <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_759">Iosif</rs>, especial-
                <lb/>ly during <rs ana="#ana_162">his difficult and bewildering "June days" in Vienna
                <lb/>and London</rs>.
              </p>
            <closer>
              <salute>
                <lb/><space quantity="4" unit="char"/>With very best wishes.
              </salute >
              <salute>
                <lb/><space quantity="24" unit="char"/>Cordially,
              </salute >
              <signed hand="#hand_blue_kline">
                <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_758">George K.</rs>
              </signed>
              <signed>
                <lb/><space quantity="24" unit="char"/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_758">George L. Kline</rs>
              </signed>
            </closer>
              <postscript>
                <ab>
                  <lb/>P.S. I greatly enjoyed your <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_554">review of the <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_794"><rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_555">Kessler</rs> diaries</rs></rs>
                  <lb/><space quantity="5" unit="char"/>in the <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_362"><hi rend="underline" hand="#type_black_kline">NYRB</hi></rs> for August 31st. The quotations from
                  <lb/><space quantity="5" unit="char"/>Kessler which you have assembled are quite fascinating.
                </ab>
                <signed hand="#hand_blue_kline">
                  -<rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_758">GLK</rs>
                </signed>
              </postscript>
              <postscript>
                <ab>
                  <lb/>Encls.
                </ab>
              </postscript>
            </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00547/" ed="2v" type="sheet"/>
            <div>
              <ab hand="#hand_blue_unident_0181">
                <lb/>51b
              </ab>
            </div>
          </div>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
